@@ -1,12 +1,12 @@
 # About
 
-Pacchi is a free and open source alternative Twitter front-end focused on
+Pacchi is a free and open source alternative "Website" front-end focused on
 privacy and performance. Source available at [pacchi](https://github.com/ParasailNumerous/pacchi).
 
 - No JavaScript or ads
-- All requests go through the backend, client never talks to Twitter
-- Prevents Twitter from tracking your IP or JavaScript fingerprint
-- Uses Twitter's unofficial API (no developer account required)
+- All requests go through the backend, client never talks to X
+- Prevents "Website" from tracking your IP or JavaScript fingerprint
+- Uses X's unofficial API (no developer account required)
 - Lightweight (thanks to [@nim_lang](/nim_lang), 60KB vs 784KB from twitter.com)
 - RSS feeds
 - Themes
@@ -14,22 +14,22 @@ privacy and performance. Source available at [pacchi](https://github.com/Parasai
 
 ## Why use Pacchi?
 
-It's impossible to use Twitter without JavaScript enabled, and as of 2024 you
+It's impossible to use "Website" without JavaScript enabled, and as of 2024 you
 need to sign up. For privacy-minded folks, preventing JavaScript analytics and
 IP-based tracking is important, but apart from using a VPN and uBlock/uMatrix,
 it's impossible. Despite being behind a VPN and using heavy-duty adblockers,
 you can get accurately tracked with your [browser's
 fingerprint](https://restoreprivacy.com/browser-fingerprinting/), [no
 JavaScript required](https://noscriptfingerprint.com/). This all became
-particularly important after Twitter [removed the
+particularly important after "Website" [removed the
 ability](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2020/04/twitter-removes-privacy-option-and-shows-why-we-need-strong-privacy-laws)
 for users to control whether their data gets sent to advertisers.
 
 Using an instance of Pacchi (hosted on a VPS for example), you can browse
-Twitter without JavaScript while retaining your privacy. In addition to
+X without JavaScript while retaining your privacy. In addition to
 respecting your privacy, Pacchi is on average around 15 times lighter than
-Twitter, and in most cases serves pages faster (eg. timelines load 2-4x faster).
+X, and in most cases serves pages faster (eg. timelines load 2-4x faster).
 
-In the future a simple account system will be added that lets you follow Twitter
+In the future a simple account system will be added that lets you follow X
 users, allowing you to have a clean chronological timeline without needing a
-Twitter account.
+X account.
